  "analysis": "The import actually succeeded - fasttext is found at /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/fasttext/__init__.py. So the issue isn't a missing module. The problem must arise when actually using it. Let me probe further - maybe it's a function-level error, or a native library issue, or a specific function that's broken.",
  "plan": "I'll test common fasttext operations: check the module's contents, try calling a function, and look at the __init__.py to understand what's exposed. I'll also check if there's a broken native extension or a shadowing issue. Let me first see what attributes are available and try a simple train/load.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python -c 'import fasttext; print(dir(fasttext))'\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python -c 'import fasttext, fasttext.util; print([x for x in dir(fasttext.util) if not x.startswith(\"_\")])'\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
