  "analysis": "Important clue: `import _fasttext` fails with ModuleNotFoundError. `_fasttext` is the compiled native extension that the pure-Python `fasttext` package wraps. The train run 'Read 0M words / Number of words: 0' confirms the native layer isn't being used. So fasttext is installed but its C extension (_fasttext) is missing or not loadable. Let me inspect the package layout to confirm and find out how FastText.py tries to import it.",
  "plan": "I'll list the site-packages/fasttext directory to see whether _fasttext (a .so) exists, and examine how FastText.py imports it. This tells me whether the extension was never built, is misnamed, or fails to load due to a missing symbol/ABI issue.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/ | grep -i fast\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/fasttext/\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n '_fasttext' /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/fasttext/FastText.py | head -n 20\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    }
